  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1139 PM CST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nA more active pattern does look to return late Monday as present\nmodel agreement continues to see our next system push across the\narea. At this time, latest ensembles are giving us around a 10 to\n35 percent chance at precipitation. However, the precipitation\ntype itself has been the biggest uncertainty of this passage.\nPresently latest model trends have continue to see the bulk of\nprecipitation occurring during the overnight hours of Monday into\nTuesday. During this time overnight low temperatures do have the\npotential to get cold enough to support a transition from rainfall\nto snowfall. However, models have been very back and forth on how\nlong we stay at or below freezing during this time. To make matter\nworse, the 540 line which is can be a good indicator of\nprecipitation type looks to shift in and out of the Panhandles\nwith each run. Regardless, any snow that does occur will have\ndifficulty sticking to surface given how warm ground temperatures\nare for this time of year. Moving on from this system does, see\nanother system attempting to move in on Thanksgiving. However,\nthere is still a lot of model disagreement with this next system\nwith chance of precipitation currently below 10 percent.\nOtherwise, look for cooler conditions to hold for the holiday week\nwith highs holding the 40s and lows near or below freezing.",
